<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Casimir II of Łęczyca</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1261–<a href="/years/1294">1294</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Casimir II of Łęczyca (c. 1261–1294) was a Polish prince of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/piast-dynasty">Piast dynasty</a>, a son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/casimir-i-of-kuyavia">Casimir I of Kuyavia</a>. After his father's death in 1267 he shared the Duchy of Brześć Kujawski with his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wladyslaw-i-lokietek">Władysław the Elbow-high</a>, and from 1288 he ruled Łęczyca. He was killed fighting Lithuanian raiders at the Battle of Trojanów in 1294.</p></div>
